@Will-zi6fn 
My point was that being scummy is normal for a corporation and there's nothing special here. 

If Nvidia has a better option, I'll buy that. If AMD has better option, I'll buy that. For me Radeon 9070XT was better.

 @samgragas8467  Like I said, there's certainly a subjective element to it, but I don't think it's that complicated and it can just be left up to the judgement of the person making the comparison. It's just a way to illustrate what's possible.

But, my main point is to specifically show what you're missing out on lower end cards like the 5050. The lower down the stack you go the fewer your options. RT is out of the question, performance level upscaling is a must, lowering textures to fit the 8GB VRAM buffer is also likely necessary. So there really aren't all that many choices.

The higher end GPUs you're comparing that against don't need to be shown with the most objectively optimal settings possible, they just need to look better enough to see the differences. Yes, some people might complain, but some people complain about everything anyway.

 @RobBCactive  The 5050 is significantly cheaper than an RTX 4060 while giving identical performance and has support for the latest NVIDIA features. That's the point.

You can all rage as much as you want, it's still gonna be the top selling card on Steam Hardware survey.

Look at the RTX 4060... everyone exploded over it and crapped it down to dirt yet it became the best GPU with 4.79%

 @alankowalski8781  The current generation is just crap and I say this having bought a RTX 5070 (a.k.a. overpriced real RTX 5060) myself.
In reality the GPU market is a monopoly where NVIDIA does whatever it pleases and AMD poorly pretends to be trying compete while just copying NVIDIA and giving consumers a price discount.
Intel is practically non-existent and will stay like that until they fix their drivers and also make GPUs with at least the same performance as AMD's and NVIDIA's latest generations.
